      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looks like there is an incompatibility between `struct host_cmd_handler_args` (legacy) and `struct ec_host_cmd_handler_args` (Zephyr).\n\nThe Zephyr version doesn\u0027t have the `result` field - so any legacy host command handlers could corrupt data.\n\nYou should add some build asserts to validate structure compatibility.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 274,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 274,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "fe28f76df448bc2ec714d9baaa21fdf3b01875a5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6bad1d3c_5adec947",
        "filename": "common/host_command.c",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 274,
      "author": {
        "id": 1438457
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-14T12:41:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, this is important topic.\n\nThe `struct ec_host_cmd_handler_args` doesn\u0027t have `result`, which is the last member in the `struct host_cmd_handler_args` structure.\n\nI\u0027ve considered 3 options:\n1. Add `#ifdef` to the definition of the `struct host_cmd_handler_args` to drop the `result` field for the upstream. The structures would be the same.\n2. Add `reserved` field to the `struct ec_host_cmd_handler_args`, as it is done for the first member `send_response`. The structures would be the same.\n3. Leave the structures different and do not use `result` while upstream.\n\nI think you are right, that the structures should stay the same, so 3. isn\u0027t a good solution. \n\nIMO, 1. is the best option. It allows catching unwanted usage of the `result`. It was my first version, but I\u0027ve changed it, because of required tests changes and forgot to change it back.\n\nPlease let me know what you think.",
      "parentUuid": "dc743abc_4eeee731",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 274,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 274,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "fe28f76df448bc2ec714d9baaa21fdf3b01875a5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
